   "format": "short_answer",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve (x^2 - 4x + 1)(y^2 + 2y) = -9, for which dy/dx = -(x - 2)(y^2 + 2y)/((x^2 - 4x + 1)(y + 1)). The tangent line to the curve is vertical at a point in the fourth quadrant. What is the x-coordinate of that point?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         2,
         [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               3
            ]
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A vertical tangent needs the denominator of dy/dx to be zero with the numerator nonzero. The denominator is zero when y = -1 or when x^2 - 4x + 1 = 0, that is x = 2 + sqrt(3) or x = 2 - sqrt(3).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            1
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = 2 + sqrt(3) or x = 2 - sqrt(3) the factor x^2 - 4x + 1 is 0, so the left side of the curve equation is 0, not -9. Neither x-value belongs to a point of the curve.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute y = -1: y^2 + 2y = -1, so x^2 - 4x + 1 = 9 and x^2 - 4x - 8 = 0, which gives x = 2 + 2 sqrt(3) or x = 2 - 2 sqrt(3).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               [
                  "Sqrt",
                  3
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "At (2 + 2 sqrt(3), -1) the numerator is -(2 sqrt(3))(-1) = 2 sqrt(3), which is nonzero, so the tangent is vertical there. That point is in the fourth quadrant, while 2 - 2 sqrt(3) is negative and puts the other point in the third. So the x-coordinate is 2 + 2 sqrt(3).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            2,
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               [
                  "Sqrt",
                  3
               ]
            ]
         ]
      }
   ],
